---
description: Never commit passwords, secrets, live IPs, or credentials
alwaysApply: true
---

# No secrets in git

Never add or commit:

- Passwords, JWT secrets, API keys, Razorpay secrets, DB credentials
- Real `.env` values (only `.env.example` with placeholders)
- Default login usernames/passwords in README or docs
- Live server IPs, private hostnames, or connection strings in README

Keep secrets in `backend/.env` (gitignored). If docs need setup steps, say "copy `.env.example` and fill in your values" — do not paste real or sample production secrets.

Do not re-add removed README credentials, JWT samples, or production IPs.
